This is expected. debci tests packages against their versions in testing.
It pulls matrix from testing and fails,

quoting relevant log:
| Selecting previously unselected package r-cran-matrix.
| Preparing to unpack .../65-r-cran-matrix_1.5-1-1_amd64.deb ...
| Unpacking r-cran-matrix (1.5-1-1) ...

> Any idea how to let the packages smoothly would be welcome.

Versioned "Depends" against rmatrix is the way to go. This[1] should
be changed to (>= 1.5-3-1~)
Please ensure that the correct version is getting pulled before you upload.

[1]: https://salsa.debian.org/r-pkg-team/r-cran-tmb/-/blob/master/debian/control#L24

